  "title": "Conscious intentions cause bodily movements",
  "statements": [
    {
      "id": "e2fb8d5a-57e4-4123-830d-66a4bb77e13d",
      "text": "Consciousness is causally efficacious. When a person decides to raise an arm and the arm goes up, the conscious intention causes it to go up, and an account of mind that cannot say so has failed.",
